  "verbalization": "Claulansine D is implicated in the interaction with Jurkat through a series of molecular pathways, with the Splicing factor, proline- and glutamine-rich acting as a central intermediary. This factor is targeted by multiple compounds, including Claulansine D, trans-Myrtanol, and Leucophleol, all of which ultimately direct their activity toward Jurkat. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism involving the regulation of splicing processes in Jurkat cells, which could influence cellular function and response. The evidence points to a possible role of Claulansine D in modulating splicing activity, potentially through the same or related pathways as the other compounds. The integration of these findings highlights a possible link between Claulansine D and Jurkat via the splicing factor, emphasizing the importance of this molecular interaction in the context of drug-target relationships.",
